From 248a67b6298df30b8fc80a5dcc95a764c81f198c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:15:32 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] STD: add predictor shim with vertical stats

Add kernel/sched/std.c and std.h with per-task history in
include/linux/sched.h alongside kernel-parameters notes. A compact
64->16->1 predictor combines deterministic s8 coefficients into s32
sums through ReLU against a threshold, using integer arithmetic in
preallocated non-sleeping wakeup context. Each task carries hist[64]
u8 plus a cursor, reset at fork. Placement prefers a fully idle core,
then any idle CPU, then spread. Deadline tasks respect a laxity veto;
real-time tasks accept only idle destinations; fair tasks consult the
predictor; idle tasks remain in place. Fastpath, steered and fallback
tallies join nn_keep, nn_migrate, split_core and constant nn_version
in a bordered vertical metric|value table with SI-1000 scaling.

Publish kernel.std_running 0644 clamped 0-1, kernel.std_nn_thresh
0644 and read-only kernel.std_stats through register_sysctl_init and
late_initcall, with std_running= and std_nn_thresh= boot parameters
described in kernel-parameters documentation.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
